{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"492423553055931673f361b6fb74533c2b6010547bab018285d416851d581bb9","digest":{"component_or_area":"DC adapter pagination structural test","key_entities":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py","test_no_search_issues_call_relies_on_the_default_page_size","adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/_base.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py","search_issues","_search_issues_calls_taking_the_default","_TRANSPORT_SRC","commit 4213081d23"],"problem_keywords":["structural guard","vacuous test","AST scan","pagination","module split","test rot"],"propositions":["The structural guard in test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py scans only transport.py but all search_issues calls were moved to _base.py and _issues.py by commit 465d, leaving the guard with zero call sites to inspect.","The guard's AST walk of transport.py returns an empty offender list, causing the assertion to pass unconditionally despite the guard's documented purpose to catch unpaginated search_issues calls.","The guard must be widened to scan all modules in adapters/jira_datacenter/ and must assert that it observes a non-zero number of search_issues call sites to prevent future rot from module relocations.","A synthetic uncapped search_issues call in a non-transport.py module must be detectable by the widened guard to prove the directory-level scan is exercised."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787889238145868001,"uuid":"f5f45f1e-91a0-4a42-acc9-e033283f32e9"}